I guess it serves a dual purpose: 1. providing a convenient way to classify
the quoted text if needed (say for computer input, or where you're
discussing several different languages at once) and 2. making sure clashes
don't occur. Since the delimiter cannot appear in the text, the idea is to
choose a delimiter that isn't. To be absolutely safe you can use a long
cmene like .supykalifrajilistikekspielydocys. but.... that is just
atrocious. *zo'o*

